model {
  extend basalt.toolsGateway {
    metadata {
      constraint "AppPages renders retained HTML with workerd's native parser and the shared portable URL, srcset and CSS rewrite policy. Attribute decoding uses the same pinned HTML parser dependency's decoder; decoding precedes URL rewriting and changed attributes escape ampersands before serialization. Native raw-text handling preserves the portable parser's bootstrap-marker behavior. Portable hosts retain their synchronous parser. AppPages supplies cryptography and path services only: remote assets and bound app runtimes require no local filesystem, process or terminal services. Production upload checks reject the portable HTML engine and those local OS modules. Cloud runtime API revisions read the shared API document directly, so AppPages does not retain the default application and management composition. Worker upload and startup budgets stay unchanged. Build aliases for workerd, parser and platform services apply only to app-pages; local test hooks remain shared and the OAuth wire mode keeps its protocol alias excluded."
    }
  }
}
